#basePath	Day1

:: OpeningCutscene
@trigger SceneReady
@cutscene
@who    IntroCutscene

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling", 1)
$call IntroCutscene->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(2)
$call TelescopeLook(155, -30)

:: ArrivalAtTheShed
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "IntroCutscene"
@cutscene
@who    Radio

$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling-Piano", 1)

{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven. Elijah, do you copy?
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} Please log in and provide status update. 

$call Wait(2)

{@Astrid} Hi—um, this is Astrid, Elijah’s ... friend. Elijah doesn't seem to be here.
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Hello?
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Ugh. They can’t hear me.
$call Wait(2)

{@Radio} Station Seven, please log in and report.

$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} I can’t, I don’t know how ...

$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} I told you, he's not there... Astrid?
$call Wait(1)
Is that you?

{@Astrid} (*gasp*) Dad! I can’t believe it's you.
Are you still at the South Pole? Are you okay?
$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} There’s not much time, so I’ll give you the short version.
My team here at IceCube has started an underground group called the STAR Coalition. We’re trying to rebuild our knowledge of the night sky. 
$call Wait(1)
It’s not easy... so much was lost during the Collapse.
$call Wait(1)
But then Elijah reached out to us. He’s onto something big...

{@Astrid} Onto what?

{@Dad} I'm so glad you're there though. We could really use your help.

{@Astrid} ... I might as well help while I wait to see if Elijah shows up.

{@Dad} I know you aren't familiar with most of that equipment, but I'll walk you through the basics.
Don't worry about clerance for the more advanced equipment, that will come in time... if you're up for it. 
First things first, we you need to submit some data the old fashioned way.
Sending you the data now...

$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(4.0)

{@Dad} OK, looks like you received the coordinates. 
{@Dad} See if you can move your telescope.

$call SetInputState(true)
$call StopMusic(2)
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("TelescopeControls", 0.4)
$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = false
$goto .MoveTelescopeReminder

:: MoveTelescopeReminder
$call Wait(10)
$if !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
    {@Dad} Still there?
     See if you can move your telescope.
    $goto .MoveTelescopeReminder
$endif
// //TODO Shake UI hint

:: MoveYourTelescope
@trigger    OnTelescopeMoved
@when   !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = true
$call HintModals->Hide("TelescopeControls", 0.2)
Nice job! Your equipment seems to be working.
See those three lights above your monitor? Feel up for a game of hot an cold?
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("NeutrinoNav", 0.4)

:: DadHotColdEncouragement1
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Nice! Getting warmer...
$call Wait(3)
{@Astrid} Remember when I was little and you used to make me find my easter basket this way?

:: DadHotColdEncouragement2
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Dad} Waaaaarrrrrmmmmmmeeerrrr!

:: DadColder1
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavColder
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Dad} Getting Colder...

:: DadColder2
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavColder
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Colder...

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call HintModals->Hide("NeutrinoNav", 0.2)
{@Dad} Nice Job! 
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StartOpenMode()
{@Dad} Early this morning, Ice Cube detected a high energy neutrino coming from one of several possible stars in this location.
You’ll see each of them highlighted on your display. 
Identifying these stars will be a great way for you get your feet wet and upgrade your system.
$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()

{@Dad} Alight. Select a possible neutrino origin on your display.
$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = true

$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("SelectStar", 0.4)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: OnStarSelected
@trigger    OnStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@cutscene
@interrupt

{@Dad} Oops.
It doesn't look like that is a possible neutrino origin.
Look for objects with a blue highlight.

:: OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@trigger    OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = false
$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = true
$call HintModals->Hide("SelectStar", 0.2)
{@Dad} Great! 
Now see if you can find Elijah’s operator manual. It should have all the info you need.

:: OnRefGuideOpened
@trigger    OnRefGuideOpened
@when   temp:waitingForManualOpen
@boostScore 200
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = false
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Dad} Do you see your photometer in the equipment stack? That should tell you what the apparent magnitude of the star is. 
All you need to do is find that number in your reference guide and submit the data.
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Dad} Hmmm, you might want to stay on target Little Bear.

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask2
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Dad} Looks like you’re drifting away from the cluster Astrid.

:: IncorrectSubmission
@trigger    OnIncorrectOpenIdSubmission

{@Dad} Hmm, looks like that wasn’t accurate. 
Remember to look at your photometer, and then line it up with the closest range in your manual.

:: DupliacteSubmission
@trigger    OnDuplicateOpenIdSubmission

{@Dad} Looks like you’ve already submitted that info. 
You won’t get any science points for identifying that property again.

:: FirstPoint
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 0
@boostScore 300
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
Fantastic Job kiddo, looks like you earned some science points!
$call Wait(1)
Ok, now try that for the rest of this cluster.
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
{@Dad} Looks like you’ve identified enough stars to earn a higher clearance level. 
You’ll need to tune to the right frequency on your radio to unlock your equipment. Tune to 375mHz.

$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("RadioControls", 0.4)

$call Wait (1)

$call HintModals->Hide("RadioControls", 0.2)

//TODO Seperate Node Here
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 2. 
You are now cleared to use the color meter. 
Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment. 

Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. 
Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow.

$call Wait(2)
{@Astrid} Huh...
$call Wait(2)

{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction...
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Awesome, your rig is upgraded! 
This time I need you to find the constellation Perseus.

{@Astrid} Perseus, huh?

{@Dad} Up for some more hot and cold?
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: DadHotColdEncouragement3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Getting waarrmer...

:: DadHotColdEncouragement4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Dad} Waaaaarrrrrmmmmmmeeerrrr!

:: DadColder3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Dad} Getting Colder...

:: DadColder4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Colder...

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)
$call StartPuzzleMode()
{@Astrid} Whoooaa...

$call Wait(1)
{@Dad} Alright kiddo, this was the.. important thing I was telling you about earlier. 
On your screen is all known information about the stars in Persius. 
I need you to input data from your gear into the identification grid that just appeared.
There should be more information in your manual.
$call SetInputState(true)

$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)

:: PerseusPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Perseus"
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Time to turn in for the night.
Oh, what's this?
$call WaitForMovedToView("Left")
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day1Martha")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: EndDay
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day1Martha"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call LoadNextDay()